[32m+[m[32m## What is GIG?[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGIG is a platform that breaks developers out of tutorial purgatory by connecting them with curated engineering tasks from real open-source repositories and business backlogs. Developers claim scoped issues, submit pull requests through standard GitHub workflows, survive maintainer code review, and earn wallet bounties — building an inspectable, evidence-backed engineering record instead of a self-declared résumé.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**For Developers:** Discover tasks filtered by stack and difficulty, lock issues exclusively for 48 hours, submit real GitHub PRs, earn reputation, and withdraw earnings via UPI.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**For Businesses:** Publish engineering work from your backlogs, review PR submissions, approve contributions, and access a pool of verified talent.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> **Status:** Alpha v0.1 — Under active development. Not yet production-ready.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **GitHub OAuth Authentication** — Sign in with GitHub, syncing profile data (bio, avatar, repos, followers)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Dual-Role System** — Separate dashboards and workflows for developers and businesses[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Issue Pool** — Browse curated tasks across opted-in repositories, filtered by technology and difficulty tier[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Task Claiming** — Lock a task exclusively for 48 hours with single-claim enforcement[m
[32m+[m[32m- **PR Submission & Review** — Submit GitHub pull request URLs; businesses review and approve/reject[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Contribution Tracking** — Verified contributions linked to actual merged PRs[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Wallet & Withdrawals** — Earned bounties tracked in an INR wallet with UPI withdrawal (₹500 minimum)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Reputation System** — 0–100 score derived from verified contributions[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Row-Level Security** — Supabase RLS policies enforce data access at the database level[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Legacy Demo Mode** — Local HMAC-based sessions for development without Supabase credentials[m
