[32m+[m[32m## Getting Started[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Prerequisites[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 20+[m
[32m+[m[32m- npm 10+[m
[32m+[m[32m- A [Supabase](https://supabase.com/) project (for production auth and database)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Installation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m# Clone the repository[m
[32m+[m[32mgit clone https://github.com/pranjal2410719/GIG.git[m
[32m+[m[32mcd GIG[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Install dependencies[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm install[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Copy environment template[m
[32m+[m[32mcp .env.example .env.local[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Configuration[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEdit `.env.local` with your credentials. See [`.env.example`](.env.example) for all available variables.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Required for Supabase auth:**[m
[32m+[m[32m| Variable | Description |[m
[32m+[m[32m|----------|-------------|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `SUPABASE_URL` | Your Supabase project URL |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase anon/publishable key (browser-safe, RLS enforced) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | Supabase service role key (server-only, bypasses RLS) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Same as `SUPABASE_URL` (exposed to client) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Same as `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (exposed to client) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `SESSION_SECRET` | HMAC session signing secret — generate with `openssl rand -base64 32` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Optional for local development without Supabase:**[m
[32m+[m[32m| Variable | Description |[m
[32m+[m[32m|----------|-------------|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `ENABLE_LEGACY_SESSION` | Set `"true"` to enable local demo login (never honored in production) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `TEST_DEV_EMAIL` / `TEST_DEV_PASSWORD` | Demo developer credentials |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `TEST_BIZ_EMAIL` / `TEST_BIZ_PASSWORD` | Demo business credentials |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Database Setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Create a Supabase project at [supabase.com](https://supabase.com)[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Run the migrations in the Supabase SQL Editor, in order:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sql[m
[32m+[m[32m-- 1. supabase/migrations/0000_init.sql          (tables + base RLS)[m
[32m+[m[32m-- 2. supabase/migrations/0001_github_profile.sql (GitHub profile columns)[m
[32m+[m[32m-- 3. supabase/migrations/0002_rls_integrity.sql  (RLS lockdown + unique constraints)[m
[32m+[m[32m-- 4. supabase/migrations/0003_rls_privilege_lockdown.sql (privilege hardening)[m
[32m+[m[32m-- 5. supabase/migrations/0004_wallet_tx_nullable_task.sql (withdrawal support)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOr push via the Supabase CLI:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run db:push[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Seed the database with demo data:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run seed[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Development[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) to see the application.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### GitHub OAuth Setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Enable **GitHub** under **Authentication → Providers** in your Supabase dashboard[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Configure the OAuth callback URL to match your `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` (e.g., `http://localhost:3000`)[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Users can sign in with GitHub on the auth page, or connect their GitHub account from the developer dashboard[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> If Supabase is not configured and `ENABLE_LEGACY_SESSION=true`, the app falls back to local demo login (`dev@gig.dev` / `biz@gig.dev`). This fallback is hard-disabled in production.[m
